# Each operator other than a path operator, alone between operands. Glyph
# 1 + 2 * K runs `100 100 rmoveto 10 20 OP 30 40 rlineto`: a line to (130, 140)
# shows OP cleared the stack, lines to (110, 120) and (140, 160) that it left
# its operands, and other boxes what it computed. Glyph 2 + 2 * K runs
# `100 100 rmoveto 50 50 rlineto 10 20 OP 30 40 rlineto`, so a failure shows
# whether what was drawn before it counts. Operators, in order: dotsection, and, or, not, abs, add, sub, div, neg, eq, drop, put, get, ifelse, random, mul, sqrt, dup, exch, index, roll, then the
# one-byte codes 0, 2, 9, 13, 15, 16, 17 and the escaped codes 12 1, 12 2, 12 6, 12 7, 12 8, 12 13, 12 16, 12 17, 12 19, 12 25, 12 31, 12 32, 12 33, 12 38, 12 39, 12 100, 12 255.
glyph
  endchar
end
glyph # dotsection
  100 100 rmoveto 10 20 dotsection 30 40 rlineto endchar
end
glyph # dotsection after a line
  100 100 rmoveto 50 50 rlineto 10 20 dotsection 30 40 rlineto endchar
end
